\end{bmatrix}
\begin{bmatrix}
x \\
y
\end{bmatrix}
=
\begin{bmatrix}
-3x \\
-3y
\end{bmatrix}
\]

Thus, the matrix that corresponds to a dilation centered at the origin with a scale factor of \(-3\) is:

\[
\boxed{\begin{bmatrix} -3 & 0 \\ 0 & -3 \end{bmatrix}}
\]

